  - Data sources (web useTranslation + the parent-supplied `annotations` prop + `onRemove`
    callback): bound through the P1/S8 seam AnnotationListSource→AnnotationListModel.
    `remove(id:)` is the native peer of `onRemove(id)`; the production source performs the
    delete + refetch, the in-memory source drops the row + re-pushes. No HTTP in the view.
  - Composition (web container + title + rows):
      • title  -> uppercase tracking-wider muted caption, web t('annotation.listTitle',
                  'Annotations'); rendered in the always-on surface header.
      • dot    -> Circle filled by AnnotationPalette.color(category) — the native peer of the
                  web ANNOTATION_COLORS hex map, expressed via design tokens (NO raw hex):
                  milestone→chartSeriesSpeed · maintenance→statusWarning · trip→statusSuccess ·
                  issue→statusDanger · upgrade→chartSeriesPower · custom→textMuted.
      • label  -> medium-weight secondary text (web font-medium).
      • desc   -> optional muted "— {description}", truncated (web hidden/sm:inline + truncate).
      • time   -> trailing muted monospaced; AnnotationFormat.timestampLabel polishes ISO-8601
                  to a localized medium-date/short-time label and passes any other string through
                  verbatim — the web renders ann.timestamp as provided.
      • remove -> AnnotationRemoveButton (xmark), always visible (web reveals on pointer-hover,
                  not portable to touch/VoiceOver), danger tint on press; web
                  t('annotation.remove','Remove annotation').
